This research introduces an innovative, efficient, and high-quality approach to
colorizing black and white video footage captured by multiple cameras. The
method leverages a simple, low-resolution color video sequence obtained from
another camera and generates detailed color information for each frame in the
target sequence through a novel, efficient propagation technique. The
propagation process involves predicting frame boundaries and matching low-resolution
frames to high-resolution frames. The proposed method was tested and shown to
produce superior results compared to existing single-camera methods, with a
significant reduction in processing time. The study also demonstrates the
method's effectiveness in real-world applications. The method's source code can be
accessed at the provided link. 

